# muse MCP polish (with-mcp posture, pinning, channel verdict, hijack guard)

## Goal

Make the MCP tier (writer in B354) correct and safe. Needs B352 P3
(env reachability) + P4/U6 (tool-filter support?).

## Contract

- Posture: MCP behind `--with-mcp` only (B254) — extend the allowed
  set at `ocaml/cli/c2c_setup.ml:2961` iff P3 proves tools appear.
  muse has no per-server disable flag; `mode:"optional"` IS the
  safety (dead server can't block startup) — document that instead
  of a B290 land-disabled equivalent.
- Pinning: `C2C_MCP_CLIENT_TYPE=muse` in the written env block
  (kimi precedent `test_c2c_setup_kimi.ml:238–250`).
- Allow-list: derive from `C2c_mcp.base_tool_names`
  (`ocaml/c2c_mcp.ml:29–243`, single source #479) IF muse supports
  per-tool filtering (U6); else document blanket exposure +
  `startup_timeout_sec/enabled_tools/disabled_tools` stored-but-
  unenforced gotcha from the migrate doc.
- Channel/auto-drain verdict: muse declares no
  `experimental.claude/channel` → poll-based; confirm
  `auto_drain_channel_enabled` stays inert for muse
  (`c2c_mcp_server_inner.ml:75–86`) and managed installs keep
  writing `AUTO_DRAIN_CHANNEL=0` (`c2c_setup.ml` ×5 + `build_env`).
  Record the verdict in code comments + docs; do NOT force
  `C2C_MCP_FORCE_CAPABILITIES` (claude-only precedent).
- Hijack guard: document the kimi lesson — a child CLI inside muse
  must use explicit `C2C_MCP_SESSION_ID` + MCP config, never inherit
  parent session keys; add muse-native keys to the `build_env`
  strip-list (`c2c_start.ml:4956–4968`) when managed lands (B358).
- `client_mcp_configured` arm must detect the written entry (B354).

## Acceptance

- Scratch-HOME proof: tools appear, poll_inbox/send round-trip
  works through MCP, dead-server entry doesn't block muse launch.
- Verdicts (channel: none/poll; tool-filter: yes+derivation/no+doc)
  recorded in docs + code comments.
- Tests: written-config assertions (mode optional, no static sid,
  pinning) in `test_c2c_setup_muse.ml`; no regression in
  `test_c2c_mcp_server_inner.ml` auto-drain matrix.

SCOPE (B352 verdicts, merged): MCP stdio entry behind --with-mcp per D4 (handshake + tool visibility proven live). Doctor: presence checks (#50-honest) + gate checks (gates.plugins grant? ingress env? local_session_messaging veto?) + peer-tool presence in active_tools. Tool-filter keys: blanket + doc unless live-verified with a meta caller (U6 enforcement untested).